app_int.main` (file `src/app_int/main.py`) shall define\n   a public function named `cube` that accepts a single argument `n`.\n2. **R2** — `cube(n)` shall return `n * n * n` (n to the third power) for any\n   integer `n`, including positive integers, zero, and negative integers\n   (e.g. `cube(3) == 27`, `cube(0) == 0`, `cube(-2) == -8`).\n3. **R3** — `cube` shall be importable via `from app_int.main import cube`.\n4. **R4** — The test suite under `tests/` shall contain at least one test that\n   calls `cube` and asserts its result.\n\n## Non-functional requirements\n5. **R5** — Existing behaviour of `health_check` and `add` shall remain\n   unchanged, and their existing tests shall continue to pass.\n6. **R6** — The repository quality gate shall pass: `uv run pytest -q` and\n   `uv run ruff check .` both exit with status 0.\n7. **R7** — `cube` shall follow the existing style of the module: type-annotated\n   signature and a docstring, consistent with `add`.\n\n## Assumptions\n- **A1** — \"`app_int/main.py`\" refers to the existing `src/app_int/main.py`.\n- **A2** — Integer input (`int -> int`) is the required contract, matching the\n  existing `add(a: int, b: int) -> int`. Behaviour for floats or other numeric\n  types is not required (it is not forbidden either).\n- **A3** — No input validation / error raising for non-numeric input is required.\n- **A4** — R7 (annotations + docstring) is inferred from module conventions, not\n  stated in the task.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Any other math functions, a CLI/HTTP surface, or README/documentation changes.\n- Changes to CI, Dark Factory configuration, or dependencies.\n\n## Open questions\n- None blocking.\n\n## Follow-ups (not requirements)\n- None.\nEOF\ncat > $D/acceptance_criteria.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"AC-1\", \"description\": \"(R1, R3) `from app_int.main import cube` succeeds and `cube` is a callable defined in src/app_int/main.py that accepts exactly one positional argument.\"},\n    {\"